1
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:04,710
I'm can't believe I'm getting my nails done.

2
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:07,420
And you said it was gonna be fun.

3
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:09,800
Which it kind of is.

4
00:00:11,170 --> 00:00:14,170
You said there were gonna be other guys. There are no other guys.

5
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:18,850
Chandler, there's a guy right over there.

6
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:18,850
That's a mailman.

7
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:21,180
That's our mailman.

8
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:23,770
Hi, how are you?

9
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:32,030
Chandler, don't worry. This doesn't make you any less of a guy.

10
00:00:32,190 --> 00:00:34,030
That does.

11
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:37,700
What am I sitting on?

12
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:43,370
Heh. I'd hate to think what this woman was scratching when this broke off.

13
00:00:43,790 --> 00:00:45,960
Know who used to have nails like that?

14
00:00:43,790 --> 00:00:45,960
No.

15
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:50,040
Oh, my God.

16
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:45,810
Joey, let me ask you a question. This has been driving me crazy.

17
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:48,310
What does this light switch do?

18
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:48,310
Oh, nothing.

19
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:51,440
Didn't it drive you crazy to not know what it did?

20
00:01:51,610 --> 00:01:53,650
I know what it did. Nothing.

21
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:58,030
They wouldn't have put it there if it didn't do something.

22
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:00,990
How can you not care?

23
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:00,990
Like this:

24
00:02:03,910 --> 00:02:05,830
Well, here's another question for you.

25
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,750
Do you know what that little silver knob on the toilet does?

26
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:11,080
Sure. It flushes it.

27
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:11,080
Okay, good.

28
00:02:11,250 --> 00:02:15,750
Now, since you know, when you come over, would you mind actually using it?

29
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:19,760
Hello.

30
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:19,760
Hey. Aah!

31
00:02:22,050 --> 00:02:24,850
Oh, my God. Wow.

32
00:02:22,050 --> 00:02:24,850
Guess who we ran into today?

33
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:29,690
Janice.

34
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:29,690
Is this amazing?

35
00:02:29,850 --> 00:02:33,020
How have you been?

36
00:02:29,850 --> 00:02:33,020
Well, um, I'm divorced.

37
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:35,020
Wow.

38
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:35,020
Really?

39
00:02:35,190 --> 00:02:37,480
Yeah, I'm riding the alimony pony.

40
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:41,990
And there it is.

41
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:45,910
I just came up to say hi. Hi.

42
00:02:47,450 --> 00:02:49,410
You, sweetie, I'll see you later.

43
00:02:47,450 --> 00:02:49,410
Okay.

44
00:02:49,580 --> 00:02:51,120
Mwah. I'll see you tonight.

45
00:02:51,290 --> 00:02:52,750
Bye. Bye.

46
00:02:51,290 --> 00:02:52,750
Bye. Bye.

47
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:55,340
Bye. Bye-bye. Bye-bye. Bye.

48
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:55,340
Bye-bye. Bye-bye. Oh.

49
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:57,130
I can't stand the woman.

50
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:01,970
What? I thought you were crazy about her.

51
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:05,510
You know all those little annoying things she did before we fell in love?

52
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:08,970
You know, like her voice and her laugh and her personality?

53
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:11,690
Well, they're all back, you know.

54
00:03:11,850 --> 00:03:14,610
And she's picked up like nine new ones.

55
00:03:14,770 --> 00:03:17,820
So, what are you doing bringing her here? There's people here.

56
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:22,280
Don't worry about it. I'm taking care of it tonight.

57
00:03:22,450 --> 00:03:25,570
You are not. You have never been able to break up with her.

58
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:27,620
Well, I don't have to break up with her.

59
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:30,450
We're not involved. I'm gonna do a preemptive strike.

60
00:03:30,620 --> 00:03:33,580
I'm gonna end it with her before it starts.

61
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:36,250
My ass is, like, frozen.

62
00:03:37,710 --> 00:03:40,460
Yeah, try sticking it in the freezer for 20 minutes.

63
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:45,390
I'm telling you.

64
00:03:52,810 --> 00:03:55,520
I can't believe you really walk alone here at night.

65
00:03:55,690 --> 00:03:58,150
I mean, you hear such stories about New York.

66
00:03:58,320 --> 00:04:00,110
No, it's really not that bad.

67
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:02,360
I mean, I, for one, feel perfectly safe.

68
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:08,280
Help! Help! Help!

69
00:04:08,450 --> 00:04:11,830
No, no, no, Ross. Ross, these are friends of mine from home.

70
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Liam, Devon, this is Ross.

71
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Oh. Heh.

72
00:04:15,170 --> 00:04:16,210
Hi, mate.

73
00:04:15,170 --> 00:04:16,210
Hey.

74
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,630
How are you, man?

75
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,630
Ha, ha.

76
00:04:17,790 --> 00:04:21,340
That was a good one, huh? I was like, "Help! Help!"

77
00:04:22,010 --> 00:04:23,010
So how are you?

78
00:04:23,170 --> 00:04:25,630
I've been meaning to ring you ever since I arrived...

79
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:28,350
...but, um, well, I've been rather busy.

80
00:04:28,510 --> 00:04:31,970
You realize we have not seen each other since the night of that U2 concert?

81
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:34,350
Ah.

82
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:34,350
Oh, my God, I think you're right.

83
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:37,940
Well, actually, the last time you and I saw each other was the next morning.

84
00:04:38,110 --> 00:04:40,320
Ha, ha. Oh, Liam.

85
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:43,490
Heh. Oh, Liam.

86
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:47,160
So, what, were you guys playing soccer or something?

87
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:48,570
Or should I call it...

88
00:04:48,740 --> 00:04:50,660
..."football"? Uh...

89
00:04:51,290 --> 00:04:53,250
We were playing rugby.

90
00:04:53,410 --> 00:04:56,790
In fact, we're playing a game tomorrow. You're welcome to play too.

91
00:04:56,960 --> 00:05:00,170
Ha, ha. Ross play rugby? I don't think so.

92
00:05:00,340 --> 00:05:02,380
Heh. What?

93
00:05:02,550 --> 00:05:04,010
What's so funny about that?

94
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:07,050
Well, I mean, you're American, to start with.

95
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:09,050
You don't really have rugby here.

96
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:14,640
Heh. Well, we didn't have freedom here until 1776 either, so...

97
00:05:14,810 --> 00:05:17,560
So good, then. We'll see you at Riverside Park at 2.

98
00:05:17,730 --> 00:05:20,110
Cheers.

99
00:05:17,730 --> 00:05:20,110
Cheers.

100
00:05:27,910 --> 00:05:32,240
Oh, boy. I just love to sing.

101
00:05:32,410 --> 00:05:33,790
Yes, I know that you do.

102
00:05:33,950 --> 00:05:36,040
One of the reasons people were complaining...

103
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:40,290
...was because most of the people had paid to hear the actor sing "Old Man River."

104
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:42,130
Oh, look at us.

105
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:46,050
Who would've thought that Cupid had a station at 14th Street Nails?

106
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:50,340
Okay, we have to talk.

107
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:55,560
I'm just getting out of a very serious relationship.

108
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:58,600
I know. And I'm just getting out of a marriage.

109
00:05:58,770 --> 00:06:01,810
I mean, talk about meant to be.

110
00:06:02,940 --> 00:06:06,320
Right. But I just think this is happening too soon.

111
00:06:06,490 --> 00:06:09,650
Oh, too soon, too schmoon.

112
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:13,280
Face it, honey, I am not letting you get away this time.

113
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:16,240
I hear you.

114
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:16,240
Ha, ha.

115
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:23,290
But unfortunately, my company...

116
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:25,960
...is transferring me overseas.

117
00:06:27,630 --> 00:06:29,880
Oh, no.

118
00:06:30,050 --> 00:06:32,140
Where to?

119
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:35,680
To Paris?

120
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:35,680
No. No, not Paris.

121
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:39,770
To London? Oh. No, Rome? Vienna? Ooh, ooh. Barcelona?

122
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:42,810
Okay, could you just stop talking for a second?

123
00:06:45,110 --> 00:06:46,320
Yemen.

124
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:52,530
That's right. Yes. I'm being transferred to Yemen.

125
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:55,780
When?

126
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:55,780
I don't know exactly.

127
00:06:57,160 --> 00:07:02,750
Well, I will just have to soak up every ounce of Chandler Bing...

128
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:06,170
...until that moment comes.

129
00:07:07,340 --> 00:07:10,130
But I do know it's sometime tomorrow.

130
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:16,140
Done?

131
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:16,140
Yep.

132
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:17,930
Hey.

133
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:17,930
Hey.

134
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:19,350
What's up?

135
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:21,520
This switch thing has been driving me crazy.

136
00:07:21,690 --> 00:07:24,020
So I turned it off and checked every outlet.

137
00:07:24,190 --> 00:07:28,280
Now, four don't work, which means one of them has to be controlled by the switch.

138
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:32,030
So I plugged in things in all four outlets that make noise.

139
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:34,740
That way, when I turn it on, I just follow the noise...

140
00:07:34,910 --> 00:07:36,740
...and find out which one it is.

141
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:40,290
I bet I stopped listening before you did.

142
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:44,210
You know, you also could have used lamps...

143
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:45,880
...and then followed the light.

144
00:07:46,590 --> 00:07:50,840
Yeah, well, I'm using noise. Okay?

145
00:07:51,010 --> 00:07:52,470
All right, so everybody ready?

146
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:55,220
Here we go.

147
00:07:57,680 --> 00:08:01,390
There's something. I hear something. Where is it?

148
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,740
It's coming from Joey.

149
00:08:15,490 --> 00:08:18,660
Oh, my God. That's so freaky. Turn him off.

150
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:25,540
With the set scrum in center field.

151
00:08:26,250 --> 00:08:27,540
Oh, hey.

152
00:08:26,250 --> 00:08:27,540
Hi.

153
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:31,130
Could we put on the news? I think it might be raining.

154
00:08:31,590 --> 00:08:35,430
No, just hold on a sec. I'm watching this rugby thing on ESPN.

155
00:08:35,590 --> 00:08:38,850
I don't know what the big deal is. I'm man enough to play this sport.

156
00:08:39,010 --> 00:08:43,020
Dude, you're not even man enough to order the channel that carries the sport.

157
00:08:44,270 --> 00:08:46,600
Hey there, Ross.

158
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:48,940
Hey.

159
00:08:49,110 --> 00:08:50,610
Janice.

160
00:08:52,610 --> 00:08:56,240
You know, uh, you really didn't have to help me pack.

161
00:08:56,410 --> 00:08:58,410
Oh. When you said all you were gonna be doing...

162
00:08:58,570 --> 00:09:00,910
...between now and the time you leave is packing...

163
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:03,290
...you really didn't leave me much choice.

164
00:09:03,450 --> 00:09:06,120
Well, I thought I did, but I guess I did not.

165
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:10,960
Hey. What's going on?

166
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:10,960
Oh, I'm packing.

167
00:09:11,130 --> 00:09:14,420
You know, I'm packing because I'm moving to Yemen tomorrow.

168
00:09:15,470 --> 00:09:16,930
Thanks for telling me.

169
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:23,470
I'm only pretend-moving to Yemen, okay? It's the only way I can get rid of her.

170
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:25,850
Oh. Good one.

171
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:30,730
And Yemen. That actually sounds like a real country.

172
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:32,980
Hey, Chandler, come on.

173
00:09:33,150 --> 00:09:36,490
I'm gonna show you how to roll your underwear and stuff it in your shoes.

174
00:09:36,650 --> 00:09:40,700
It's a real space-saver.

175
00:09:36,650 --> 00:09:40,700
I do that because it makes me look taller.

176
00:09:42,540 --> 00:09:45,040
Hey, Chandler. Come on.

177
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,290
Okay.

178
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:49,080
Joey, trade lives with me.

179
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:49,080
Nope.

180
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,840
Man, look at this. Ross, I can't believe you said you'd play.

181
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:56,800
Look how brutal this is.

182
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:56,800
Hey, I can handle it, all right?

183
00:09:56,970 --> 00:09:58,090
Oh, please, Ross.

184
00:09:58,260 --> 00:10:02,300
You got hurt playing badminton with my dad.

185
00:10:02,470 --> 00:10:06,060
That's because your mom's dog kept looking at me.

186
00:10:07,850 --> 00:10:11,190
Okay, Ross, look, look, look. Right here, it's called a "scrum," okay?

187
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:15,320
It's kind of like a huddle.

188
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:15,320
And is a hum kind of like a scruddle?

189
00:10:16,690 --> 00:10:19,150
Ross, they're gonna kill you.

190
00:10:21,160 --> 00:10:22,910
Why are you doing this, anyway?

191
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:26,620
Well, you should've seen the guy that she used to go out with.

192
00:10:26,790 --> 00:10:28,960
I mean, he's like Joe Rugby.

193
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:32,330
You're kidding. And he plays rugby? That's so funny.

194
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:36,500
Oh, I see. You did that. All right.

195
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:42,550
Anyway, she thought the very idea of me playing rugby with him was, like, hilarious.

196
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:45,260
So I'm gonna show her how tough I really am.

197
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:51,190
I'm sorry, I'm sorry. You're right. You are a tough guy.

198
00:10:51,350 --> 00:10:53,560
You're the toughest paleontologist I know.

199
00:10:54,230 --> 00:10:55,230
All right, come on.

200
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:58,740
Look, Ross can take care of himself. It's not like he's Chandler.

201
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:00,570
Thanks.

202
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,700
Look, don't worry about me.

203
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:06,410
I'll just look real energetic and stay away from the ball.

204
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:08,750
I'll be that guy, right outside the circle.

205
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:11,710
Ooh.

206
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:11,710
Oh!

207
00:11:11,870 --> 00:11:14,210
Oh, jeez.

208
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:18,090
Oh. Well, maybe there was a dog looking at him.

209
00:11:26,810 --> 00:11:28,100
Okay, Ross, Ross, Ross.

210
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:31,600
You're gonna wanna stay away from that guy and that guy and that one.

211
00:11:31,770 --> 00:11:34,230
Dude, they're all huge.

212
00:11:35,110 --> 00:11:36,770
They don't look any bigger than me.

213
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:38,780
That's because you're closer to you.

214
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:40,990
So you look bigger to you from where you are.

215
00:11:43,030 --> 00:11:45,030
I'm just gonna go and say hello to the lads.

216
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:46,950
All right.

217
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:46,950
Okay.

218
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:51,370
Hi.

219
00:11:51,540 --> 00:11:52,660
Oh.

220
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:56,000
I kind of liked it.

221
00:11:57,710 --> 00:12:01,090
Okay, I know what I've gotta do. I've gotta go Red Ross.

222
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:05,470
You know, Red Ross?

223
00:12:05,640 --> 00:12:07,680
Totally don't know what you're talking about.

224
00:12:07,850 --> 00:12:10,970
That time that we were all waiting in line for Dances With Wolves...

225
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:14,310
...and that one guy cut in front of us, and I just lost it?

226
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:17,770
Huh? Screamed at him, turned all red.

227
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:19,400
Red Ross!

228
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:22,070
No.

229
00:12:22,780 --> 00:12:24,490
You'll see.

230
00:12:25,530 --> 00:12:27,320
Liam, do me a favor.

231
00:12:27,490 --> 00:12:30,660
Tell the lads to go easy on Ross. It's his first time.

232
00:12:31,450 --> 00:12:32,580
You don't say?

233
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:41,090
Thanks.

234
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:41,090
Okay.

235
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,840
Good luck, babe.

236
00:12:44,010 --> 00:12:46,380
Ross. Ross, come on, get in here.

237
00:12:48,350 --> 00:12:50,350
Ross, come on.

238
00:12:56,190 --> 00:12:57,520
Ross.

239
00:12:57,690 --> 00:12:59,770
Ross, come on, get in the bloody scrum.

240
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:02,190
Ross, get in.

241
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:15,460
Joey!

242
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:21,920
Oh. You are not gonna believe it. Joshua came in today, and guess what.

243
00:13:22,090 --> 00:13:23,550
He asked you out?

244
00:13:22,090 --> 00:13:23,550
No.

245
00:13:23,710 --> 00:13:27,630
But I was showing him some cuff links, and I felt his pulse.

246
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:31,510
Saucy.

247
00:13:32,430 --> 00:13:36,230
What are these?

248
00:13:32,430 --> 00:13:36,230
Oh. Electrical plans for the building.

249
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:40,100
Okay, okay, okay, should I be scared?

250
00:13:40,270 --> 00:13:44,230
I know that switch has gotta do something. So I went to City Hall and I got these.

251
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:47,200
All I had to do was pay $25 and wait in line for three hours.

252
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:50,820
Wow. If only more people knew.

253
00:14:03,250 --> 00:14:06,670
You know, you really didn't have to take me to the airport.

254
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:09,930
Oh, please. Every moment is precious.

255
00:14:10,090 --> 00:14:13,220
Besides, somebody had to ride in that other taxi with your luggage.

256
00:14:13,390 --> 00:14:16,560
And your friends don't seem to care very much that you're leaving.

257
00:14:17,430 --> 00:14:19,060
Well, we're not really that close.

258
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:24,270
Okay. So I guess this is, uh, you know, goodbye, then.

259
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:25,820
Oh, no, no.

260
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:28,990
It's not goodbye. I'm not leaving until you get on that plane.

261
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:33,700
Okay, well, I guess it's just "wait here," then.

262
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:39,080
Hi. I need a fake ticket to Yemen.

263
00:14:40,330 --> 00:14:42,750
One ticket to Yemen?

264
00:14:40,330 --> 00:14:42,750
Oh, no, no, no.

265
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:45,460
I just need a pretend ticket.

266
00:14:45,630 --> 00:14:47,670
I'm sorry, sir, I don't understand.

267
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:50,840
What would you give to a kid if he wanted a ticket to play with?

268
00:14:51,010 --> 00:14:53,510
Are you traveling with a child?

269
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:56,430
No.

270
00:14:57,680 --> 00:15:00,770
Oh. She's gonna think that I'm handing you a credit card.

271
00:15:00,940 --> 00:15:04,730
But what I'm really gonna do is hand you a library card.

272
00:15:05,190 --> 00:15:10,860
Uh, sir, a ticket to Yemen is $2100, and we don't take library cards.

273
00:15:11,490 --> 00:15:13,870
What's the matter? Is something wrong?

274
00:15:14,490 --> 00:15:16,030
Do you have to stay?

275
00:15:17,660 --> 00:15:19,700
American Express?

276
00:15:23,790 --> 00:15:25,880
Ross!

277
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:33,720
I can't believe they're doing that to him. I told them to go easy on him.

278
00:15:33,890 --> 00:15:36,350
No offense, but sometimes it's hard to understand you...

279
00:15:36,510 --> 00:15:38,430
...you know, with the accent, so...

280
00:15:40,140 --> 00:15:42,440
That's just halftime. There's more of this.

281
00:15:40,140 --> 00:15:42,440
Oh.

282
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:43,650
Hey.

283
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:43,650
Hey.

284
00:15:43,810 --> 00:15:45,190
Hey.

285
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:49,980
Did you see me? I was pretty good, huh? That is one fun game.

286
00:15:50,150 --> 00:15:52,950
Right.

287
00:15:50,150 --> 00:15:52,950
Do me a favor? Grab me a bottle of water?

288
00:15:53,110 --> 00:15:54,860
Yeah.

289
00:15:53,110 --> 00:15:54,860
Thanks.

290
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:59,830
I think I'm dying. I really do.

291
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:59,830
Oh, poor baby.

292
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,790
Tell my son that I love him.

293
00:16:03,250 --> 00:16:06,580
Oh, excellent. Okay, gotta have some more fun.

294
00:16:06,750 --> 00:16:08,500
Ross, they are killing you out there.

295
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:13,260
That's not true.

296
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:13,260
She's right. You have to stop.

297
00:16:13,430 --> 00:16:16,590
What? No. No, I'm not stopping. I'm Red Ross.

298
00:16:16,760 --> 00:16:19,970
Dude, you go back out there, you're gonna be Dead Ross.

299
00:16:20,140 --> 00:16:23,390
I don't care. I am not quitting. I am gonna finish this game.

300
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:26,560
All right. If you insist on doing this, at least let me help you.

301
00:16:26,730 --> 00:16:30,780
God, no. That is no place for a woman. Those guys will grab anything.

302
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:33,240
That's not what I was saying.

303
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:36,610
I just might know a few things that could help you inflict some pain.

304
00:16:36,780 --> 00:16:40,160
I like that.

305
00:16:36,780 --> 00:16:40,160
Yeah? Listen closely.

306
00:16:40,330 --> 00:16:42,410
Devon has got a weak ankle.

307
00:16:40,330 --> 00:16:42,410
Huh?

308
00:16:42,580 --> 00:16:44,660
One swift kick and he'll back off.

309
00:16:44,830 --> 00:16:46,580
All right, bad ankle. Got it.

310
00:16:46,750 --> 00:16:48,670
And that big bloke with the beard?

311
00:16:46,750 --> 00:16:48,670
Uh-huh.

312
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:50,590
He's got a trick hip.

313
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:50,590
Ha, ha.

314
00:16:50,750 --> 00:16:54,630
Yeah. And David over there, I heard that he doesn't wear a cup.

315
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:58,050
Real...? I could use that. Trick hip, no cup. Okay, okay.

316
00:16:58,260 --> 00:17:00,810
And Liam. Liam's got bad knees.

317
00:17:00,970 --> 00:17:03,180
You hit him right and he'll go down like a lamp.

318
00:17:03,350 --> 00:17:05,060
But Liam's on my team.

319
00:17:05,230 --> 00:17:08,270
I don't care. You just get him.

320
00:17:05,230 --> 00:17:08,270
Go get him.

321
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:11,480
Okay. I am going back in.

322
00:17:13,990 --> 00:17:17,320
Red Ross. Yeah.

323
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:22,120
Hi.

324
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:22,120
Hi.

325
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:27,580
What are these?

326
00:17:27,750 --> 00:17:31,130
Oh, just some pictures I made and hung up.

327
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:34,510
I thought they'd brighten up the place. They do, don't you think?

328
00:17:37,130 --> 00:17:39,180
Aah!

329
00:17:37,130 --> 00:17:39,180
No, no, don't, don't.

330
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:41,350
Oh!

331
00:17:43,350 --> 00:17:46,640
I know that there's no hole there. I just really like that picture.

332
00:17:49,310 --> 00:17:51,690
Oh, my God. Look at this.

333
00:17:51,860 --> 00:17:55,320
But there is a wire back there. That switch is connected to something.

334
00:17:55,490 --> 00:17:59,410
I don't care. The wires have come loose in your head.

335
00:17:59,820 --> 00:18:02,910
I thought if I could follow the wire, I could find out what it did.

336
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:06,000
And did you?

337
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:06,000
No.

338
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:08,540
It disappears back behind that baseboard.

339
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,670
For a minute there, I thought it went downstairs.

340
00:18:16,380 --> 00:18:18,170
But it didn't.

341
00:18:19,510 --> 00:18:22,760
Say hello to Mrs. Catrokis.

342
00:18:19,510 --> 00:18:22,760
Oh, my God.

343
00:18:22,930 --> 00:18:26,810
Hello, darling.

344
00:18:22,930 --> 00:18:26,810
Hello, Mrs. Catrokis.

345
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:33,610
Are you sure you don't wanna go see a doctor?

346
00:18:33,770 --> 00:18:36,940
Oh, no, that'll just bring me down.

347
00:18:37,110 --> 00:18:41,240
This was great. I mean, I was great. This was a great day.

348
00:18:41,410 --> 00:18:43,870
You know what? I'm buying everyone coffee.

349
00:18:44,030 --> 00:18:46,160
Someone just grab my wallet. It's in my pocket.

350
00:18:46,330 --> 00:18:47,500
Yeah, sure.

351
00:18:46,330 --> 00:18:47,500
No, not you.

352
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:49,120
Okay.

353
00:18:49,580 --> 00:18:52,880
Look, your eye's still popping out a little. I'm gonna go get some ice.

354
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:55,630
Okay.

355
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:55,630
Ooh, ice, yeah. I'm so in the mood for ice.

356
00:18:58,050 --> 00:19:00,590
You were amazing out there.

357
00:18:58,050 --> 00:19:00,590
Oh.

358
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:03,470
I kind of was, wasn't I?

359
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:03,470
Oh, my God.

360
00:19:03,640 --> 00:19:07,810
I made a man twice my size cry.

361
00:19:07,980 --> 00:19:12,850
I mean, I haven't done that since I was 4 and I washed my dad's Porsche with rocks.

362
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:16,820
You really enjoyed yourself, didn't you?

363
00:19:16,980 --> 00:19:19,740
Please, are you kidding? I hurt three huge men.

364
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:21,740
I gave a guy a bloody nose.

365
00:19:21,910 --> 00:19:24,490
I mean, I'm not proud of it...

366
00:19:24,990 --> 00:19:26,490
...but I really am.

367
00:19:27,910 --> 00:19:29,910
And it's all because of you.

368
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:34,830
Yeah. Wonderful, amazing you.

369
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:34,830
I think you've got a concussion.

370
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,590
No, no, I'm serious. Thank you.

371
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:40,800
You're welcome.

372
00:19:42,930 --> 00:19:46,140
I'm sorry. Did that hurt you?

373
00:19:42,930 --> 00:19:46,140
It's worth the pain.

374
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:50,020
You know what? You know what? It's not.

375
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:59,780
This is the final boarding call for Flight 664 to Yemen.

376
00:20:02,740 --> 00:20:04,450
Well, I guess I gotta go.

377
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:07,580
Oh. My Bing-a-ling.

378
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:10,830
I'll wait for you.

379
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,120
Do you even know how long you're gonna be gone?

380
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:19,500
Well, just until we find an energy source to replace fuel.

381
00:20:19,920 --> 00:20:23,840
Oh. Well, I'll write you every day.

382
00:20:24,010 --> 00:20:27,140
15 Yemen Road, Yemen.

383
00:20:28,850 --> 00:20:31,060
Okay. Goodbye.

384
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:32,810
Goodbye.

385
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:47,320
Chandler?

386
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:47,320
No.

387
00:20:47,490 --> 00:20:49,280
Chandler.

388
00:20:49,450 --> 00:20:52,660
Janice. There you are. There you are. I had to have one last kiss.

389
00:20:52,830 --> 00:20:56,500
And also, also, you said you were gonna leave right after I got on the plane.

390
00:20:57,290 --> 00:21:00,880
No. No. I wanna see you take off.

391
00:21:01,670 --> 00:21:04,050
Well, then I guess I'm going to Yemen.

392
00:21:06,010 --> 00:21:08,180
I'm going to Yemen.

393
00:21:09,350 --> 00:21:12,890
When we get to Yemen, can I stay with you?

394
00:21:19,650 --> 00:21:22,940
All right. The super couldn't figure out what it did.

395
00:21:23,110 --> 00:21:27,150
The $200-an-hour electrician couldn't figure out what it did.

396
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:30,530
I've had seven pretty serious shocks.

397
00:21:31,370 --> 00:21:34,410
I officially give up.

398
00:21:31,370 --> 00:21:34,410
Thank God.

399
00:21:35,370 --> 00:21:37,370
I guess Joey was right.

400
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:39,830
It does nothing.

401
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:46,300
See?

402
00:21:50,220 --> 00:21:54,060
I'm doing it. I am totally doing it.

403
00:22:00,900 --> 00:22:02,730
I lost it.

